$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=tm2lfes  LOC_AFTER=?

* The entry loop ` forEntries ` of TM/Lists.lean with a per-entry cost family: from the entry peek, through the loop, to the exit with the loop test cleared and the list reduced to its ` bra ` , within ` sum_ j e. ( 0 ..^ ( # ` L ) ) ( ( Y ` j ) + 2 ) + 2 ` steps.  ~ tm2lfe is the uniform case.  Lean: ` forEntries_runs' ` (PrimList.lean; ` forEntriesN_runs' ` at ` L := ( encNatGam o. l ) `), the rule of ` divisorsOfF ` whose body costs grow with the entry index.

